Source: bibata-cursor-theme
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), fdupes [!i386]
# ^ fdupes is dedup-only (cosmetic, cursors install fine without it); the
# OBS xUbuntu i386 pool does not provide it (proven 2026-10-11: bibata
# i386 unresolvable on `nothing provides fdupes`), so it is restricted
# off i386 and debian/rules skips it when absent.
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/ful1e5/Bibata_Cursor

Package: bibata-cursor-theme
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, hicolor-icon-theme
Description: Open source, compact, and material designed cursor set
 Bibata is an open source, compact, and material designed cursor set
 that aims to improve the cursor experience.
